# Dogfooding workspace & local WIP — dev clone only, never published
/Virtuoso/
# Anchored on purpose. A dev clone's repository-root .codex-plugin/ is local WIP and
# stays out of the repo; plugins/virtuoso/.codex-plugin/ is the shipped alternate-host
# manifest and must not match. An unanchored `.codex-plugin/` ignores both, and
# deleting it un-ignores both -- which put local WIP in front of release.py's
# clean-tree gate on every dev clone that had one.
/.codex-plugin/
.superpowers/
.claude/
